{"request": {"input_type": "document", "model": "voyage-4", "text": "A customer success lead explains how the team keeps customer emails consistent, mainly through reused onboarding templates whose welcome email promises exactly the two training sessions in the Onboarding Pack, then describes the plain, jargon-free tone suited to small and mid-sized customer firms, and finally says what they wish sales would do differently: record every promise in the CRM.\n\nInterviewer: How do you keep emails consistent across the team?\n\nCustomer success lead: We reuse a few templates for onboarding. The Onboarding Pack includes two training sessions, and our welcome email says exactly that, nothing more. People used to promise unlimited training to be nice, and then we could not deliver.\n\nInterviewer: Anything about tone that is specific to your customers?\n\nCustomer success lead: Our customers are mostly small and mid-sized firms, so we avoid jargon. Write like you would explain it to a smart colleague from another department. Short sentences, active voice.\n\nInterviewer: What do you wish sales did differently?\n\nCustomer success lead: Write down what they promised. Half of my onboarding calls start with \"but the salesperson said\". If it is not in the CRM, I cannot honor it."}, "vector": [0.026339218020439148, -0.006985080894082785, -0.001224570325575769, -0.021237365901470184, 0.053776953369379044, -0.009430420584976673, -0.0274873748421669, -0.0039064837619662285, 0.03181992471218109, 0.05563955008983612, 0.0068572694435715675, 0.0727449581027031, -0.015215392224490643, 0.03856322169303894, -0.023543432354927063, 0.012948407791554928, 0.01500740833580494, -1.6382720787078142e-05, 0.03127589821815491, 0.02806110307574272, 0.023167859762907028, 0.07992338389158249, -0.003827526932582259, -0.0020012101158499718, 0.02025155909359455, 9.328240366812679e-07, -0.0014425622066482902, 0.03297918662428856, -0.053261324763298035, -0.027175238355994225, -0.017279060557484627, 0.0